                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_125\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit changes `ArenaListener.onFoodLevelChange`:\n\n    if (arena.isRunning()) {\n-       if (lockFoodLevel) {\n+       if (arena.inArena(p) && lockFoodLevel) {\n            event.setCancelled(true);\n        }\n    } else {\n\ni.e. it adds a missing `arena.inArena(p)` check so that the food-level lock only applies to players who are actually in the arena, instead of everyone on the server while the arena is running.\n\ncandidate_125 is a refactor of the exact same method. Before this commit, `onFoodLevelChange` began with:\n\n    if (!arena.isRunning()) return;\n    if (!(event.getEntity() instanceof Player) || !arena.inArena((Player) event.getEntity())) return;\n    if (lockFoodLevel) event.setCancelled(true);\n\nwhich correctly guarded the lock behind an `inArena` check. candidate_125 restructured this to add lobby/spectator handling (per its changelog entry \"Food levels no longer deplete for players in the lobby and spectator area\"), but in doing so it dropped the `inArena` check from the `arena.isRunning()` branch entirely:\n\n    if (!(event.getEntity() instanceof Player)) return;\n    Player p = (Player) event.getEntity();\n    if (arena.isRunning()) {\n        if (lockFoodLevel) {\n            event.setCancelled(true);\n        }\n    } else {\n        if (arena.inLobby(p) || arena.inSpec(p)) {\n            event.setCancelled(true);\n        }\n    }\n\nThis is precisely the buggy code the fix commit later patches by adding back `arena.inArena(p) &&` to the `isRunning()` branch. No candidate between 125 and the fix reintroduces or removes this check (candidate_128 is the fix itself, mistakenly included among the diffs, and only re-adds the missing check). Therefore candidate_125 is the commit that introduced the bug.\n"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
